      "title": "PROFESSIONAL AUDIO PADDING: PREROLL, POSTROLL & HANDLES",
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.8",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "⏱️ PROFESSIONAL AUDIO PADDING: PREROLL, POSTROLL & HANDLES\n\nWhy do we use the 'Empty Audio' and 'Audio Concat' nodes to inject 5 seconds of silence? \nIn the professional VFX and film industry, this is a vital quality-gate workflow:\n\n1. PREROLL (The 2.5s Buffer at the Start)\n*   Nodes: 'Empty Audio' (2.5s) -> Connected to 'Audio Concat' (direction: before)\n*   VFX Purpose: Acts as a stabilization buffer for the KSampler. It gives the \n    Float Advanced engine temporal room to calibrate its latent coordinates \n    on Frame 0, completely preventing sudden mouth-warping glitches [🔍].\n\n2. POSTROLL (The 2.5s Buffer at the End)\n*   Nodes: 'Empty Audio' (2.5s) -> Connected to 'Audio Concat' (direction: after)\n*   VFX Purpose: Acts as a natural anatomical cool-down. It allows the latent \n    engine to organically close the avatar's lower jaw after the final word \n    is spoken, preventing the face from freezing abruptly.\n\n3. HANDLES (The Post-Production Benefit)\n*   Result: Compiled via 'IndexTTS2 Save Audio' into a 26-second master track.\n*   VFX Purpose: Provides essential \"editing handles\" (flesh on the bone) for \n    your NLE software (like DaVinci Resolve or CapCut) [🔍]. This ensures you can \n    apply smooth cross-fades and cuts without clipping the voice [🔍].\n\n"
      ],
      "color": "#323",
      "bgcolor": "#535"
    },
